WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.040
Ammonia leak.

2
00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.040
What to do when the alarm sounds.

3
00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:09.091
Outside the station, pipes full of ammonia
carry the heat away.

4
00:00:09.131 --> 00:00:12.331
It works great, but ammonia is toxic to
breathe.

5
00:00:13.231 --> 00:00:14.892
In January twenty fifteen,

6
00:00:14.892 --> 00:00:18.532
an alarm sent the whole crew out of the
American segment.

7
00:00:18.572 --> 00:00:22.753
Within minutes, everyone was in the
Russian segment, with the hatch closed.

8
00:00:23.653 --> 00:00:27.818
It turned out to be a false alarm, and the
procedure worked perfectly.

9
00:00:28.718 --> 00:00:32.392
If the ammonia alarm sounds, put on your
mask right away.

10
00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.917
Don't wait to smell it: trust the alarm.

11
00:00:35.817 --> 00:00:39.196
Move to the safe segment, and close the
hatch behind you.

12
00:00:39.236 --> 00:00:42.306
Every crew member knows where the safe
segment is.

13
00:00:43.206 --> 00:00:47.613
Burning eyes or throat? Rinse with plenty
of water, and tell Keiko.

14
00:00:48.513 --> 00:00:50.565
Mask first, questions later.

